                <pb facs="0198" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/17.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Hill to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-04-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to department’s April 16, Ambassador Hill says formalities for transit
                    from Germany are the same as extradition from that country, and that an agent
                    can not accompany fugitive on board German vessel or through Germany.</p>
            </div>
